adjudication.rationale:
The diff changes `_hydrateEmbedded` to treat keys ending in `_ids` as arrays:

```js
if (m[2]) {
  const hydrated = obj[k].map(function(id) {
    return self._lookupSubType(subType, type, id, root);
  });
  obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
  delete obj[k];
}
```

This introduces a verifiable correctness issue: it unconditionally calls `.map` on `obj[k]`, so if the server sends `null`/non-array for an `_ids` field, this will throw at runtime. Also, unlike the singular `_id` branch (which only assigns when `hydrated` is truthy), the array branch will keep `undefined` entries when `_lookupSubType` can’t resolve an id, producing arrays with holes/undefined values without any filtering. The “no JS unit test” part is true (no tests added here), but the real defect is the unguarded `.map` and potential undefined elements.
